    - Keep the anchor at its input position and translate the other sprites only.
    - Attach sprites by making red ports coincide with currently unpaired red ports in the growing assembly.
    - Red-on-red overlap is the only allowed overlap; body-colored pixels may never cover any occupied cell.

    Key insight: Once body color stops distinguishing pieces, the puzzle is solved entirely by geometry: bbox shape, port placement, and the invariant that every red connector must be paired exactly once.
    """
    g = np.asarray(grid, dtype=int)
    h, w = g.shape
    bg = 0

    pieces = _extract_pieces(g, bg)
    assert pieces, "input must have at least one colored piece"

    # Anchor is the unique piece containing the yellow (color 4) core block.
    anchors = [p for p in pieces if np.any(p["arr"] == 4)]
    assert len(anchors) == 1, "input must have exactly one yellow (4) anchor piece"
    anchor = anchors[0]
    rest = [p for p in pieces if p is not anchor]

